      "id": "01",
      "characterId": "mira-mask",
      "identityNameBase": "Mira Mask",
      "subject": "raccoon",
      "scientificName": "Procyon lotor",
      "observationId": 121268871,
      "photoId": 205171222,
      "title": "Out of reach",
      "theme": "movement",
      "body": "Reached down to see what was under the water. Couldn't find it.\n\nPut the other paw in. Still nothing.\n\nThen the bank began moving past me.\n\nHad to stop looking for the bottom and use both hands to swim back.",
      "visible": "Wet raccoon in open water, head and curved back above the surface, tail trailing upward; driftwood and stems around it. Companion frame shows the same animal farther from the woody margin.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Reaching, momentary loss of contact with the bottom, drifting before noticing and swimming back are fiction. The photographer describes a swim on a hot afternoon, but submerged feet and exact depth are not visible. Do not claim that either frame proves paddling, current speed or danger. The moving bank is the narrator noticing her own movement, not a literal moving shore.",
      "canon": "Existing female Mira, adult-sized scene after her explicit childhood water memory. Preserve Great Smoky Mountains stream forest (35.62, -83.47), adult avatar and all literal bodies. Source Lake Avalon, New Mexico is provenance, not travel. This is not the held flat-stone flood story: her tactile investigation must become propulsion when she loses the bottom. No injury or rescue.",
      "flag": "Selected closer frame is moderately soft but the wet animal and open-water relationship are clear. Exact body position may also be wading; the proposed prior loss of bottom is an invented sequence, not a source diagnosis.",
      "platform": "instagram",
      "contentType": "story",
      "status": "proposal_pending_lead_review",
      "mediaSha1": "26334aa7154b08d652e36cde0a7079782204f1cd",
      "localPath": "/tmp/freed-land111/205171222.jpg"
    },
    {
      "id": "02",
      "characterId": "nessa-whisker",
      "identityNameBase": "Nessa Whisker",
      "subject": "Arctic fox",
      "scientificName": "Vulpes lagopus",
      "observationId": 377181918,
      "photoId": 689704160,
      "title": "From down here",
      "theme": "social",
      "body": "She leapt at me. I ducked.\n\nShe went over my head and landed in the flowers. Came straight back.\n\nDucked again.\n\nI had wanted a chase. Now I'm staying in one place while she does all the running, and I can't make myself spoil it.",
      "visible": "Two dark juvenile Arctic foxes playing in a meadow with pale pink flowers. Left fox rises toward the lower right fox with front legs extended. Both mouths are open. Companion frame shows both foxes facing one another on the ground.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Source explicitly identifies two playing juveniles. Nessa is fictional lower fox; the other fox is unnamed, sex and kinship unrecorded. Flying over her head, repeated ducking and enjoying the arrangement are fictional timing and intention. Neither frame proves a complete jump or the relationship. No adult dark-morph inference.",
      "canon": "Existing female Nessa. Insert this juvenile memory before the adult Calling through a fly Story and adult seasonal-coat episodes. Keep Svalbard tundra coast (78.15, 15.25), current white adult avatar, existing sister and old literal drafts. Iceland is source provenance, not a move. Young Arctic foxes can be dark regardless of adult morph; no switch to a permanently dark adult is proposed. This is not another Rufus landing on a sibling: the lower animal repeatedly evades contact and lets the chase become a stationary game.",
      "flag": "The pair are small within a broad flowered meadow, but their separate poses and relationship read clearly. The leap-over sequence is fiction. Lead should judge whether the stationary-game payoff is sufficiently distinct from admitted juvenile fox play elsewhere.",
      "platform": "instagram",
      "contentType": "story",
      "status": "proposal_pending_lead_review",
      "mediaSha1": "a160238d48bc5acdc202e3151f44d8bd0a909fcc",
      "localPath": "/tmp/freed-land111/689704160.jpg"
    }
